@startuml usdk_uagent_components
' Reconciles the task-supplied starting architecture (five capabilities -
' LLM, voice, vision, accessibility, robotics - dynamically loaded inside
' a browser environment, connected to a core system) with the actual
' package names, dependency edges, and loading mechanism as built - see
' docs/UAGENT_ARCHITECTURE.md and docs/UAGENT_PACKAGES.md for the prose
' this diagram summarizes. The two-role split below (host-browser vs.
' host-local) and the dynamic-vs-static-import distinction are new
' engineering for this project, not present in the original prompt's
' component sketch, which did not distinguish an execution profile.
'
' RENDERING UNVERIFIED: no local PlantUML CLI or plantuml.jar+Java was
' found anywhere in this environment (checked directly - see
' docs/VALIDATION.md); per this task's own instruction, this .puml
' source ships as-is rather than downloading rendering tooling.

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam backgroundColor white

package "packages/contracts" as contracts {
  [Candidate / Vote / Status types]
}

package "packages/core" as core {
  [Core: round state machine]
  [MemoryJournal / FileJournal]
}

package "packages/loader" as loader {
  [ManifestRegistry: resolve()]
  [loadPlan(): dynamic import()]
}

package "Three roles (statically imported)" {
  [perceive] as perceive
  [deliberate] as deliberate
  [verify] as verify
}

package "Five capability contracts" {
  [capability-llm]
  [capability-voice]
  [capability-vision]
  [capability-a11y]
  [capability-robotics]
}

package "Drivers (dynamically import()-ed by name)" as drivers {
  [driver-llm-fixture]
  [driver-llm-local]
  [driver-voice]
  [driver-vision]
  [driver-robotics-sim]
}

package "Browser-local profile" {
  [host-browser: ConversationSession] as hostbrowser
  [uagent: index.html / app.mjs] as uagentbrowserlocal
}

package "Connected profile" {
  [host-local: HTTP+JSON server] as hostlocal
  [binding-javascript: ConnectedSession] as bindingjs
  [uagent: connected.html / connected.mjs] as uagentconnected
  [usdk.exe (native CLI, spawned)] as usdkexe
}

package "Other language bindings (local process only)" {
  [binding-python: ctypes] as bindingpy
  [binding-lua: LuaJIT FFI] as bindinglua
}

contracts <.. core
contracts <.. loader
contracts <.. perceive
contracts <.. deliberate
contracts <.. verify
contracts <.. "capability-llm"
contracts <.. "capability-voice"
contracts <.. "capability-vision"
contracts <.. "capability-a11y"
contracts <.. "capability-robotics"

"capability-llm" <.. "driver-llm-fixture"
"capability-llm" <.. "driver-llm-local"
"capability-voice" <.. "driver-voice"
"capability-vision" <.. "driver-vision"
"capability-robotics" <.. "driver-robotics-sim"

hostbrowser --> core : constructs
hostbrowser --> loader : resolve() + loadPlan()
hostbrowser --> perceive : static import
hostbrowser --> deliberate : static import
hostbrowser --> verify : static import
loader ..> drivers : dynamic import()\n(manifest entry path)
deliberate ..> "driver-llm-fixture" : injected (DI),\nnever imported directly
core ..> "driver-voice" : dispatch fn (post-commit only)
core ..> "driver-robotics-sim" : dispatch fn (post-commit only)

uagentbrowserlocal --> hostbrowser : constructs, in-tab

hostlocal --> hostbrowser : reuses ConversationSession\nunmodified (Node)
hostlocal --> usdkexe : execFile (argv array,\nno shell) for\n/native/doctor,/native/inspect
bindingjs --> hostlocal : fetch() over HTTP\n(pairing secret,\nbearer token,\nOrigin allowlist)
uagentconnected --> bindingjs : constructs

usdkexe ..> "native usdk_perceive.dll\nusdk_deliberate.dll\nusdk_verify.dll" : LoadLibraryExW/dlopen\n(real dynamic C-ABI loading)

bindingpy ..> "native usdk_perceive.dll\nlibusdk_contracts.dll" : ctypes.CDLL\n(direct, in-process)
bindinglua ..> "native usdk_perceive.dll\nlibusdk_contracts.dll" : LuaJIT ffi.load\n(direct, in-process -\nUNTESTED, no runtime\navailable in this environment)

note right of hostlocal
  Connected mode requires, per task
  instruction: explicit pairing secret
  (printed to host-local's own console,
  never embedded in browser code),
  Origin allowlist, per-session bearer
  token, a fixed server-side manifest
  set (never client-supplied), and a
  usdk.exe module allowlist for
  /native/inspect - see
  docs/UAGENT_ARCHITECTURE.md
  "Browser and native boundaries".
end note

note bottom of drivers
  Only driver-robotics-sim ships -
  simulated, no physical hardware.
  driver-llm-fixture labels every
  response "[fixture] ... not real
  model inference" - see
  docs/UAGENT_ARCHITECTURE.md
  "Do not present fixture responses
  as real model inference."
end note

@enduml
